# Teramind Access Token (JWT, generated in the Teramind dashboard ->
# Administrator/User menu -> Access Tokens). Passed to Teramind's API in the
# x-access-token header.
#
# IMPORTANT (see README's "Credential scope" section): a token inherits the
# FULL permissions of whichever account created it. By default (a single
# Administrator account, the common case for a fresh self-serve trial) a
# token can reach every endpoint in Teramind's API, including screen
# recordings, keystroke logs, and email/chat content capture - this
# connector's own code never calls those endpoints, but the credential
# itself is not restricted unless you deliberately create the token under a
# reduced-privilege account (Operational Administrator - see README).
TERAMIND_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Per-instance Teramind API base URL, e.g. https://yourcompany.teramind.co
# (cloud) or your on-premise dashboard's URL. Teramind's API is scoped per
# customer instance - there is no shared multi-tenant base URL.
TERAMIND_INSTANCE_URL=
